1
00:00:02,335 --> 00:00:03,711
- Where is she?
- Over here.

2
00:00:04,128 --> 00:00:05,171
You saw the suspect?

3
00:00:05,296 --> 00:00:07,089
Details, please. Where? When?

4
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,592
Uh, I was coming out
of the elevator after lunch.

5
00:00:09,759 --> 00:00:11,052
Where was the suspect headed?

6
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,970
Uh, up the stairs, which I thought
was strange

7
00:00:13,137 --> 00:00:14,222
'cause that leads to the roof, right?

8
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:15,973
It's not just the roof.
It's where Jane works.

9
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:17,892
- Has anybody seen him?
- Not since this morning.

10
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:19,769
Cover the exits! All of them!

11
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:21,729
Use whoever you have to out here!

12
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:30,154
Hasten slowly.
The target will be armed.

13
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:51,717
It's locked.

14
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:53,970
Jane?

15
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:57,473
- You in there?
- "Yeah, I'm coming out."

16
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:03,771
"You're gonna have to stand back.
And if you're bearing firearms"

17
00:01:03,896 --> 00:01:05,273
"please lower them."

18
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:07,316
"Please."

19
00:01:23,916 --> 00:01:25,084
Stand back...

20
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:26,877
or he dies.

21
00:02:01,702 --> 00:02:04,997
{\an8}Security guard making rounds this morning
found the body. Multiple stab wounds.

22
00:02:05,164 --> 00:02:06,624
{\an8}Anything missing from the display case?

23
00:02:06,749 --> 00:02:08,667
{\an8}Yeah, a Mayan figurine. Gold.

24
00:02:08,834 --> 00:02:10,002
{\an8}Valued at 200 grand.

25
00:02:10,252 --> 00:02:13,005
{\an8}- We get an I.D. on the victim?
- Manuel Montero.

26
00:02:13,297 --> 00:02:15,549
{\an8}He was a professor at the university
in ancient art.

27
00:02:15,674 --> 00:02:17,259
{\an8}Security cameras show him
entering the museum alone

28
00:02:17,384 --> 00:02:18,510
at 10:25 p.m.

29
00:02:18,802 --> 00:02:20,512
{\an8}- then he turned off the cameras.
- "Hey, Lisbon."

30
00:02:21,055 --> 00:02:22,097
{\an8}Look at this.

31
00:02:23,974 --> 00:02:25,017
{\an8}Meet Caroline...

32
00:02:25,726 --> 00:02:29,480
{\an8}one of the most well-preserved
tyrannosaurus rex ever discovered.

33
00:02:29,688 --> 00:02:32,441
{\an8}- Isn't she awesome?
- We've got a dead man over there.

34
00:02:32,691 --> 00:02:36,820
{\an8}- Dead men I've seen. But this...
- Could we get back to work, please?

35
00:02:38,947 --> 00:02:41,241
{\an8}Must I justify my every action?

36
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:46,121
{\an8}Please observe the rib cage
of our smaller fossilized friend here.

37
00:02:46,914 --> 00:02:48,832
- Is there a rib broken off?
- Exactly.

38
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:51,293
You think somebody climbed up
there and stole it?

39
00:02:51,627 --> 00:02:53,962
{\an8}Well, two options...
the first involves cloning.

40
00:02:54,088 --> 00:02:55,339
{\an8}The second and more likely...

41
00:02:55,464 --> 00:02:57,925
{\an8}it was used to break a very thick
piece of glass.

42
00:02:59,927 --> 00:03:02,596
{\an8}Could we get somebody to dust
the stegosaurus for prints, please?

43
00:03:03,222 --> 00:03:05,641
{\an8}It's not a stegosaurus. It's a triceratops.

44
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:09,978
{\an8}- Triceratop... s. Ps.
- S. Ps.

45
00:03:10,729 --> 00:03:14,066
{\an8}My name is Christo Papadakis.
I am professor of anthropology.

46
00:03:14,191 --> 00:03:16,026
{\an8}- Did you know the victim?
- Manuel Montero.

47
00:03:16,151 --> 00:03:19,405
{\an8}He was part-time faculty.
Too busy to teach full-time.

48
00:03:19,947 --> 00:03:21,407
{\an8}Montero was on the run.

49
00:03:21,782 --> 00:03:22,825
{\an8}On the run from who?

50
00:03:23,826 --> 00:03:25,285
{\an8}Nobody. He... he traveled.

51
00:03:25,411 --> 00:03:27,454
{\an8}He was always running to South America.

52
00:03:29,123 --> 00:03:32,126
- His career was in ruins.
- Well, tough times for everybody.

53
00:03:32,334 --> 00:03:34,169
Not for Montero.
He had a lot of money.

54
00:03:34,336 --> 00:03:36,088
Well, you just said he was in ruins.

55
00:03:37,005 --> 00:03:39,341
Yes, Toltec. Mayan.

56
00:03:39,758 --> 00:03:41,260
Oh. Montero was an archaeologist?

57
00:03:41,427 --> 00:03:43,303
Specializing in Pre-Columbian Art.

58
00:03:43,429 --> 00:03:47,015
Many of the pieces around you are,
uh, on loan from him.

59
00:03:47,307 --> 00:03:49,309
Can you think of anyone
with a reason to kill Montero?

60
00:03:50,310 --> 00:03:53,272
- Well, he was a traitor and...
- Oh, he was a traitor?

61
00:03:53,439 --> 00:03:54,481
Who did he betray?

62
00:03:54,857 --> 00:03:56,984
- Betray? Nobody.
- Well, you just said he was a...

63
00:03:57,109 --> 00:04:00,612
Montero was an honest antiquities dealer.
One of the last.

64
00:04:01,321 --> 00:04:04,950
Most traders these days are looters
and no-good son-of-a-bitches.

65
00:04:05,659 --> 00:04:08,495
So, Montero was a trader...

66
00:04:08,746 --> 00:04:15,335
He traded antiquities, excavated
from South American ruins.

67
00:04:17,504 --> 00:04:20,132
Are you really professional
police officer?

68
00:04:24,887 --> 00:04:26,805
So the missing pendant
belonged to the victim.

69
00:04:27,055 --> 00:04:28,599
Montero liked to visit
the museum after hours

70
00:04:28,724 --> 00:04:30,476
to show his pieces to private buyers.

71
00:04:30,726 --> 00:04:32,936
He had a key to the building
and the security code.

72
00:04:33,854 --> 00:04:36,774
At the heart of any salesman
is showmanship.

73
00:04:36,899 --> 00:04:40,110
And you'd be hard-pressed to find
a more dramatic proscenium than this.

74
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:42,571
Yeah, smart strategy unless
the buyer doesn't wanna pay.

75
00:04:42,946 --> 00:04:44,656
Stabbed in the back, literally.

76
00:04:45,532 --> 00:04:47,117
Montero probably didn't even
see it coming.

77
00:04:47,367 --> 00:04:49,203
But he had time to think
about it before he died.

78
00:04:49,328 --> 00:04:50,412
Look at his watch.

79
00:04:52,372 --> 00:04:53,874
Wow. That's an ugly watch.

80
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:55,876
- It's a calculator watch.
- Indeed.

81
00:04:56,043 --> 00:04:58,921
Very useful accessory
for the sales pro on the go.

82
00:04:59,379 --> 00:05:00,631
Is there something typed in there?

83
00:05:02,382 --> 00:05:04,426
It's uh, numbers.

84
00:05:04,718 --> 00:05:07,846
"6-0-7-8."

85
00:05:08,263 --> 00:05:09,306
Supposed to mean something?

86
00:05:09,681 --> 00:05:11,642
Try looking at the numbers upside-down.

87
00:05:15,813 --> 00:05:16,855
It says "Blog".

88
00:05:17,272 --> 00:05:19,316
His cell phone was crushed by the killer

89
00:05:19,525 --> 00:05:21,860
so Montero here improvised.

90
00:05:22,027 --> 00:05:24,696
Call Van Pelt
and see if Montero published a blog.

91
00:05:25,322 --> 00:05:27,491
- I'm ready to go. I've seen enough.
- I haven't.

92
00:05:28,075 --> 00:05:31,119
You know they have mastodons here?
Giant sloths.

93
00:05:31,578 --> 00:05:34,081
And dire wolves. I-I'll catch up.

94
00:05:34,873 --> 00:05:37,167
"But, Mommy, I wanna go."

95
00:05:37,292 --> 00:05:41,088
You can squawk all you like, Mimi.
There's no sleepovers on a school night.

96
00:05:41,213 --> 00:05:43,590
- "I have to."
- No.

97
00:05:44,091 --> 00:05:45,884
"Mommy, that's unfair."

98
00:05:46,677 --> 00:05:47,970
I'm sorry, baby. I gotta go.

99
00:05:48,679 --> 00:05:51,807
- "All right. Love you. Bye."
- Love you, too. Bye.

100
00:05:54,268 --> 00:05:55,477
Forgive the intrusion.

101
00:05:58,021 --> 00:05:59,773
What's this about, Agent LaRoche?

102
00:06:05,112 --> 00:06:07,948
The Todd Johnson case.

103
00:06:12,703 --> 00:06:15,247
I would like to show you a photo

104
00:06:15,914 --> 00:06:18,667
of one of the law enforcement officers

105
00:06:19,501 --> 00:06:22,129
that he murdered.

106
00:06:27,801 --> 00:06:29,386
Did you know this man?

107
00:06:31,054 --> 00:06:33,599
Rance Howard.
C.H.P. officer.

108
00:06:34,516 --> 00:06:36,852
Very popular.
A lot of our agents were close to him.

109
00:06:37,227 --> 00:06:38,604
Some more than others.

110
00:06:42,816 --> 00:06:47,195
There's a rumor that you and Howard
were intimately involved.

111
00:06:47,863 --> 00:06:48,906
Is that true?

112
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,200
- Excuse me?
- Simple question.

113
00:06:52,701 --> 00:06:53,869
Simple answer...

114
00:06:54,202 --> 00:06:56,455
what the hell is that to you
or anybody else?

115
00:06:57,164 --> 00:06:59,750
Johnson was set on fire...

116
00:07:00,918 --> 00:07:03,170
a crime of passion
if there ever was one.

117
00:07:04,671 --> 00:07:09,051
If you were having an affair
with one of Johnson's victims

118
00:07:09,718 --> 00:07:13,180
you had passion and motive.

119
00:07:18,644 --> 00:07:20,479
Your investigation seems to hinge

120
00:07:20,687 --> 00:07:23,565
on what you may have read
on a bathroom wall.

121
00:07:26,944 --> 00:07:28,862
Good luck with that, Agent LaRoche.

122
00:08:08,777 --> 00:08:10,821
- Background on Montero.
- What do we know about him?

123
00:08:10,988 --> 00:08:13,865
Single, self-employed, spent half his time
abroad importing ancient art.

124
00:08:14,032 --> 00:08:16,076
- Sold it from a warehouse in San Francisco.
- Family?

125
00:08:16,410 --> 00:08:18,412
Parents retired in Florida.
They'll be on the next flight here.

126
00:08:18,537 --> 00:08:20,330
Hey, boss. I looked into the blog.

127
00:08:20,455 --> 00:08:23,291
Montero did publish one...
"I dig dead people."

128
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,461
Archaeology humor. Cute.
Anything useful?

129
00:08:26,795 --> 00:08:30,048
A lot of self-promotional entries
about his relic-hunting adventures.

130
00:08:30,173 --> 00:08:33,135
But three weeks ago
he came back from a trip to Columbia

131
00:08:33,301 --> 00:08:35,262
with the gold pendant that was stolen
from the museum.

132
00:08:35,512 --> 00:08:36,930
After Montero blogged about it

133
00:08:37,055 --> 00:08:40,767
a private buyer posted an anonymous
e-mail to arrange a viewing.

134
00:08:41,059 --> 00:08:42,352
Did you put a trace on the e-mail?

135
00:08:42,602 --> 00:08:44,813
Not me. FBI's computer forensics lab.

136
00:08:44,938 --> 00:08:47,149
One of the perks of having a fiancé
with the Feds.

137
00:08:47,733 --> 00:08:49,317
Preliminary forensic report.

138
00:08:49,484 --> 00:08:51,903
You're gonna have dozens of prints
from the triceratops skeleton.

139
00:08:52,070 --> 00:08:53,530
It's gonna take a while
to process them, though.

140
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,533
While we're waiting on forensics,
let's work on developing some leads.

141
00:08:56,658 --> 00:08:58,285
Hey, you said that Montero
had a warehouse?

142
00:08:58,452 --> 00:08:59,745
Yeah, in the Mission District.

143
00:08:59,995 --> 00:09:01,872
But there's something else.
I ran his financials.

144
00:09:02,122 --> 00:09:03,915
The profits from his company
have been going up at a time

145
00:09:04,041 --> 00:09:06,043
when other art and antiquity
dealers are closing shop.

146
00:09:06,293 --> 00:09:08,336
- Closing shop? Why?
- Repatriation laws.

147
00:09:08,462 --> 00:09:10,589
Countries are now suing for the return
of their cultural treasures.

148
00:09:10,839 --> 00:09:13,508
You and Rigsby go to the warehouse.
See if you can find anything.

149
00:09:13,633 --> 00:09:15,010
Alright.

150
00:09:22,684 --> 00:09:23,894
- Hi, Jane.
- Hey.

151
00:09:24,061 --> 00:09:25,604
The boys are working
on the parking lot today.

152
00:09:25,729 --> 00:09:27,856
- Need you to park underground.
- Oh, no problem.

153
00:09:28,231 --> 00:09:31,443
That kid of yours, Jim... Is he
into dinosaurs and prehistoric stuff?

154
00:09:31,777 --> 00:09:32,819
Sure loves his mother.

155
00:09:34,404 --> 00:09:35,697
Here. Give him this.

156
00:09:36,073 --> 00:09:38,033
It's a replica of a dire wolf's tooth.

157
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:40,827
Thanks. Look at that.

158
00:09:41,661 --> 00:09:42,704
Have a good day.

159
00:10:19,908 --> 00:10:21,827
- What?
- I didn't say anything.

160
00:10:22,661 --> 00:10:23,870
You were thinking it.

161
00:10:24,287 --> 00:10:26,373
- Mentalizing me.
- You can tell?

162
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,376
I can read it on your face.
So stop.

163
00:10:29,709 --> 00:10:32,462
Well, if you can read it on my face,
then you're mentalizing me.

164
00:10:32,587 --> 00:10:33,672
So you stop.

165
00:10:34,256 --> 00:10:37,008
Oh. No, on second thought, keep going.

166
00:10:37,175 --> 00:10:39,052
- What am I thinking?
- Please go away, Jane.

167
00:10:39,177 --> 00:10:40,679
Nope. That's wrong. Try again.

168
00:10:41,930 --> 00:10:43,849
You're thinking I'm freaking out

169
00:10:43,974 --> 00:10:46,560
because some fool spread a rumor

170
00:10:46,685 --> 00:10:48,854
that I was having an affair
with Rance Howard.

171
00:10:49,062 --> 00:10:50,313
The C.H.P. officer?

172
00:10:50,438 --> 00:10:51,648
You're the one thinking it.

173
00:10:51,982 --> 00:10:53,024
I feel naked.

174
00:10:54,818 --> 00:10:57,612
There's only one person that has this
singular effect on people.

175
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,781
You've been LaRoched, haven't you?

176
00:11:01,533 --> 00:11:03,910
- I suppose I have.
- Well, there's no shame in it.

177
00:11:04,077 --> 00:11:05,537
We're all pots in his kitchen.

178
00:11:05,829 --> 00:11:08,832
And he's a sous-chef
just waiting for one of us to boil over.

179
00:11:09,082 --> 00:11:10,750
I won't give him the satisfaction.

180
00:11:11,042 --> 00:11:13,628
- Of course not. Did you?
- Did I what?

181
00:11:13,795 --> 00:11:15,463
Did you have an affair
with Rance Howard?

182
00:11:16,214 --> 00:11:18,425
My personal life is my personal life.

183
00:11:19,301 --> 00:11:21,136
Nobody else has the right to it.

184
00:11:21,386 --> 00:11:23,346
Well you're wrong about that.
LaRoche does.

185
00:11:23,722 --> 00:11:26,224
Whatever the truth is
I wouldn't try to hide it from him.

186
00:11:26,892 --> 00:11:28,185
He'll find out eventually.

187
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:38,320
It's our lucky day, buddy.

188
00:11:38,653 --> 00:11:40,530
See that taco truck
just as we got off the freeway?

189
00:11:40,655 --> 00:11:42,449
- That taco truck's always there.
- Oh, yeah.

190
00:11:42,616 --> 00:11:45,160
A little carne asada after we check
out the warehouse?

191
00:11:45,327 --> 00:11:46,453
- "Super good."
- No.

192
00:11:47,329 --> 00:11:48,371
Why not?

193
00:11:48,496 --> 00:11:50,290
I don't wanna cross hobo alley
to order lunch from a truck

194
00:11:50,415 --> 00:11:52,083
that's near the sewage ditch
under the freeway.

195
00:11:53,043 --> 00:11:54,211
But there's tacos there.

196
00:11:56,504 --> 00:11:57,547
This is the warehouse.

197
00:12:03,136 --> 00:12:04,179
Let's check out the back.

198
00:12:10,518 --> 00:12:11,561
Hey!

199
00:12:14,231 --> 00:12:16,399
CBI. Who's in charge here?

200
00:12:17,025 --> 00:12:20,862
"Estamos con la policía.
Quién está a cargo?"

201
00:12:22,948 --> 00:12:24,282
Maybe they don't speak Spanish.

202
00:12:24,574 --> 00:12:25,617
Maybe you don't.

203
00:12:26,785 --> 00:12:28,078
You guys work for Montero?

204
00:12:31,289 --> 00:12:32,332
Gun!

205
00:12:48,348 --> 00:12:49,391
Cover me!

206
00:13:08,868 --> 00:13:10,161
"Idiot."

207
00:13:10,996 --> 00:13:12,205
Throw out your weapon!

208
00:13:12,747 --> 00:13:13,915
"La Pistola!"

209
00:13:14,582 --> 00:13:15,625
Do it now!

210
00:13:21,047 --> 00:13:23,800
Step into clear view!
Hands in the air!

211
00:13:32,934 --> 00:13:35,312
Face down on the ground.
Hands out to your sides. Do it now.

212
00:13:41,151 --> 00:13:43,153
Hey! Hey, hey, easy! Easy!

213
00:13:43,278 --> 00:13:45,488
Yeah, now he understands English.
So...

214
00:13:46,156 --> 00:13:48,366
What kinda ancient art you boys
selling today, huh?

215
00:14:06,591 --> 00:14:07,759
Roberto Salvador.

216
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:10,136
You're on a work visa from Columbia.

217
00:14:11,429 --> 00:14:12,638
So you work for Montero?

218
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:17,060
Could be.
Could be Montero work for me.

219
00:14:19,103 --> 00:14:20,271
Attitude. Really?

220
00:14:23,316 --> 00:14:24,650
Uh, where are you going?

221
00:14:25,526 --> 00:14:27,320
To write you up on charges
of running guns

222
00:14:27,445 --> 00:14:29,113
resisting arrest, attempted murder...

223
00:14:29,322 --> 00:14:31,199
"Hey, hey, calm down."

224
00:14:33,451 --> 00:14:35,161
I only shot at you
because you shot at me.

225
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:37,830
What... what can I do here?
I got a family, you know.

226
00:14:38,206 --> 00:14:39,248
I wanna see them again.

227
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,501
You answer my questions.
No attitude.

228
00:14:41,667 --> 00:14:43,252
Maybe we'll forget
about the attempted murder.

229
00:14:44,712 --> 00:14:46,589
Good. Sit down.

230
00:14:47,382 --> 00:14:48,424
Put your feet up.

231
00:14:51,636 --> 00:14:52,845
Why did Montero hire you?

232
00:14:53,513 --> 00:14:56,307
- To run his shipping operation.
- Weapons or antiquities?

233
00:14:56,974 --> 00:14:58,017
Both.

234
00:14:58,309 --> 00:15:00,186
Manuel was an honest businessman
for many years

235
00:15:00,311 --> 00:15:02,605
but the profit in those museum
pieces went away.

236
00:15:02,814 --> 00:15:04,565
Too many legal barriers.

237
00:15:04,816 --> 00:15:07,443
Politicians, criminals to bribe.

238
00:15:07,693 --> 00:15:09,445
So Montero started trafficking guns.

239
00:15:10,238 --> 00:15:11,572
He had his company all set up.

240
00:15:11,948 --> 00:15:14,158
He could ship them to South America,
no questions asked

241
00:15:14,283 --> 00:15:17,036
then trade them for all the black
market antiquities he could handle.

242
00:15:17,662 --> 00:15:19,038
Did Montero have any enemies?

243
00:15:19,747 --> 00:15:22,166
No. He was beloved.

244
00:15:22,417 --> 00:15:25,002
In Colombia, they called him
"El Profesor."

245
00:15:25,628 --> 00:15:26,671
What do you think?

246
00:15:26,838 --> 00:15:30,675
Well, it has a certain pulp appeal
as far as mysteries go...

247
00:15:31,259 --> 00:15:33,428
murder in the museum,
stolen Mayan gold

248
00:15:33,553 --> 00:15:34,846
Colombian gun runners...

249
00:15:35,179 --> 00:15:37,014
But it's a tawdry work of fiction

250
00:15:37,807 --> 00:15:39,142
completely made up.

251
00:15:39,267 --> 00:15:41,269
Oh, I'm pretty sure Montero's dead.

252
00:15:41,561 --> 00:15:44,105
Yes, but not for the reasons
that we're being led to believe.

253
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:45,273
How can you tell?

254
00:15:46,274 --> 00:15:48,025
I find it easier to show than to tell.

255
00:15:49,610 --> 00:15:50,778
Uh, excuse me.

256
00:15:51,821 --> 00:15:54,157
Could you please tell me
who Montero was trading weapons to

257
00:15:54,282 --> 00:15:55,324
in South America?

258
00:15:56,409 --> 00:15:57,452
Answer the question.

259
00:15:57,994 --> 00:16:01,205
- Cartels, gangs, private armies.
- Oh, makes sense.

260
00:16:01,873 --> 00:16:04,625
If they wanted him dead,
how would they go about that?

261
00:16:04,917 --> 00:16:07,253
You would never know how.
He would just...

262
00:16:08,004 --> 00:16:09,046
disappear.

263
00:16:09,297 --> 00:16:10,381
Okay.

264
00:16:10,756 --> 00:16:14,135
And if the body just happened
to be found miraculously

265
00:16:14,594 --> 00:16:15,720
where might that be?

266
00:16:15,970 --> 00:16:18,306
Uh, a mass grave. Side of a road.

267
00:16:19,182 --> 00:16:22,310
We found him stabbed
and bled out in a public museum.

268
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:24,145
Would you kill a man that way?

269
00:16:24,395 --> 00:16:26,606
Hell, no. Heh. Too high-risk.

270
00:16:30,610 --> 00:16:33,154
Somebody killed Montero for reasons

271
00:16:33,321 --> 00:16:35,281
that had nothing to do
with Pre-Columbian art

272
00:16:35,448 --> 00:16:38,159
and nothing to do
with Colombian cartels.

273
00:16:38,367 --> 00:16:40,703
That's just what the killer
wanted us to think.

274
00:16:42,914 --> 00:16:44,957
Oh, I asked Conway
over at Gambling Control

275
00:16:45,082 --> 00:16:47,376
to join our investigation
into the loan-shark syndicate.

276
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:50,421
Conway's a good man,
but he can talk the paint off a car.

277
00:16:50,546 --> 00:16:51,714
Don't let him run the briefings.

278
00:16:51,923 --> 00:16:54,592
- Director Bertram.
- J.J., you waiting for me?

279
00:16:56,010 --> 00:16:57,678
Special Agent Hightower, actually.

280
00:17:07,355 --> 00:17:08,898
- Good night.
- Night.

281
00:17:13,444 --> 00:17:15,571
A visual reconstruction

282
00:17:15,696 --> 00:17:17,740
of the night of Todd Johnson's murder

283
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:20,493
based on security footage

284
00:17:21,077 --> 00:17:22,370
activity logs

285
00:17:22,912 --> 00:17:25,081
and 86 hours of interviews.

286
00:17:26,457 --> 00:17:27,792
Nice project board.

287
00:17:29,335 --> 00:17:31,170
Bet you won a few science fairs.

288
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,260
I won all of them.

289
00:17:42,598 --> 00:17:46,018
This is the holding cell
where Johnson was burned alive.

290
00:17:46,477 --> 00:17:47,728
The circles indicate

291
00:17:48,271 --> 00:17:50,231
the location of people within CBI

292
00:17:50,398 --> 00:17:52,942
moments before his murder.

293
00:17:54,694 --> 00:17:56,821
My research revealed

294
00:17:56,946 --> 00:18:00,533
that this group of people did not
have the security clearance

295
00:18:01,075 --> 00:18:03,035
to enter the holding area.

296
00:18:07,915 --> 00:18:09,417
This group...

297
00:18:10,543 --> 00:18:13,129
they were all too far away
to have set the fire.

298
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:16,632
These...

299
00:18:17,967 --> 00:18:22,346
all have at least two or more witnesses
who can verify

300
00:18:22,930 --> 00:18:26,017
their location at the time of the attack.

301
00:18:30,855 --> 00:18:31,897
Five circles.

302
00:18:36,277 --> 00:18:39,488
- This one is you.
- Is it?

303
00:18:41,407 --> 00:18:42,783
I offer you this...

304
00:18:44,285 --> 00:18:45,620
Five suspects...

305
00:18:46,203 --> 00:18:49,081
within striking distance of Johnson

306
00:18:50,458 --> 00:18:53,336
each one highly capable

307
00:18:55,338 --> 00:18:56,589
but only one...

308
00:18:57,798 --> 00:18:59,133
with a clear motive.

309
00:19:00,509 --> 00:19:01,552
Okay.

310
00:19:03,721 --> 00:19:04,764
Okay.

311
00:19:05,431 --> 00:19:07,308
I was sleeping with Officer Howard.

312
00:19:09,268 --> 00:19:10,853
But I didn't...

313
00:19:12,396 --> 00:19:13,439
I-I...

314
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,986
At the time Howard was killed,
we were no longer together.

315
00:19:19,403 --> 00:19:21,864
- His choice or yours?
- Mutual decision.

316
00:19:22,073 --> 00:19:23,407
It... It... It wasn't...

317
00:19:26,619 --> 00:19:31,457
- Did you set Todd Johnson on fire?
- No, I did not.

318
00:19:35,753 --> 00:19:36,796
You must have been...

319
00:19:38,339 --> 00:19:39,382
grieving

320
00:19:40,049 --> 00:19:41,550
about Howard.

321
00:19:43,803 --> 00:19:45,221
How did you deal with that?

322
00:19:46,555 --> 00:19:50,643
I got on my knees and I asked the Lord
for strength and forgiveness.

323
00:19:50,810 --> 00:19:52,603
That's how I dealt with that.

324
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,566
You might wanna write that down.

325
00:20:00,027 --> 00:20:01,362
I think I'll remember it.

326
00:20:10,663 --> 00:20:11,956
"Hey, Jane. You were right."

327
00:20:12,081 --> 00:20:15,042
Well, of course. What instance
of rightness are we speaking of?

328
00:20:15,167 --> 00:20:17,545
Yesterday, when you said
Montero was killed for reasons

329
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:19,463
having nothing to do
with the stolen artifacts.

330
00:20:19,630 --> 00:20:22,758
So I stayed up late last night
and I researched his personal life.

331
00:20:22,925 --> 00:20:24,593
Someone should stay up
and research yours.

332
00:20:24,969 --> 00:20:26,011
You're never gonna guess
where he grew up.

333
00:20:26,137 --> 00:20:27,179
Then I won't even try.

334
00:20:27,304 --> 00:20:28,347
- Vineland, California.
- Vineland, California.

335
00:20:28,472 --> 00:20:30,683
- How did you do that?
- I followed your lips. Vineland?

336
00:20:31,392 --> 00:20:33,853
Hometown of infamous cop killer
Todd Johnson?

337
00:20:34,186 --> 00:20:35,229
Follow me.

338
00:20:38,524 --> 00:20:40,276
Did you print that photo
I sent you last night?

339
00:20:40,401 --> 00:20:42,027
Yep. That's Johnson and Montero.

340
00:20:42,153 --> 00:20:44,113
They were co-captains of their
high school football team.

341
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:45,322
Are you getting this?

342
00:20:45,531 --> 00:20:48,492
Our murder victim was best friends
with the serial cop killer.

343
00:20:49,285 --> 00:20:50,327
It's a great photo.

344
00:20:51,036 --> 00:20:54,540
After I put that together I asked Cho
to go to Montero's warehouse last night

345
00:20:54,665 --> 00:20:56,250
see if he could find any other links.

346
00:20:56,709 --> 00:20:57,752
Tell him what you found.

347
00:20:57,877 --> 00:21:00,171
The guns Montero was running?
He bought them from gun shops.

348
00:21:00,421 --> 00:21:02,298
Paid people with clean records
to make the buys.

349
00:21:02,465 --> 00:21:05,217
Montero has a record of every
purchase, including serial numbers.

350
00:21:05,426 --> 00:21:07,052
Let me guess. You traced
one of the serial numbers

351
00:21:07,178 --> 00:21:09,555
back to a weapon that Montero
gave to his buddy Johnson.

352
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:12,224
That's right. Same weapon
Johnson used to kill his victims.

353
00:21:15,561 --> 00:21:17,563
Have you mentioned
any of this to LaRoche?

354
00:21:17,897 --> 00:21:20,316
I set a briefing
with top brass in ten minutes.

355
00:21:20,858 --> 00:21:23,194
LaRoche, Bertram, and Hightower
will all be there.

356
00:21:23,736 --> 00:21:25,112
- Ten minutes, Cho.
- Yep.

357
00:21:34,872 --> 00:21:37,500
Uh, excuse me.
I'm looking for the fingerprint lab.

358
00:21:38,292 --> 00:21:40,044
That's... that's me. Who are... you?

359
00:21:41,170 --> 00:21:42,213
Patrick Jane.

360
00:21:42,338 --> 00:21:44,632
Any luck with the curious case
of the triceratops rib?

361
00:21:46,801 --> 00:21:48,177
Look, I don't really...

362
00:21:48,803 --> 00:21:51,639
function efficiently under pressure,
so...

363
00:21:51,806 --> 00:21:55,100
Hey, no pressure. Just wondering
if you'd found any matches yet.

364
00:21:55,476 --> 00:21:59,146
Well, I've scanned a total of 32 full
and partial prints from that fossil

365
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:03,734
but for every print that I scan,
dozens of possible matches...

366
00:22:04,443 --> 00:22:06,362
come back. Then I have to check them

367
00:22:06,779 --> 00:22:09,698
manually one by one to find a match,
so...

368
00:22:10,282 --> 00:22:12,701
You know, I'm not David Caruso.
It takes time.

369
00:22:12,952 --> 00:22:16,163
Well, you do your thing. I'm just gonna
take a quick peek at your list

370
00:22:16,288 --> 00:22:17,331
if you don't mind.

371
00:22:24,672 --> 00:22:26,465
Push hard on this one.
We need a rapid response.

372
00:22:26,590 --> 00:22:28,968
Remember, any time
wasted's gone forever.

373
00:22:29,343 --> 00:22:31,303
I'm not wasting time.

374
00:22:32,012 --> 00:22:33,889
Are you suggesting
you don't have enough time?

375
00:22:34,223 --> 00:22:37,142
You have exactly the same number
of hours in the day

376
00:22:37,268 --> 00:22:38,769
that Albert Einstein had.

377
00:22:39,061 --> 00:22:40,563
- Can you stop?
- Thomas Jefferson.

378
00:22:40,938 --> 00:22:42,231
Louis Pasteur.

379
00:22:42,815 --> 00:22:46,402
- Gandhi.
- Just get out of... here. Oh, my God!

380
00:22:46,569 --> 00:22:48,070
Oh, my God. What do I do?

381
00:22:51,031 --> 00:22:53,158
- What do I do? What do I do...
- Keep up the good work.

382
00:22:55,369 --> 00:22:58,497
Montero was found at the archeology
museum with stab wounds.

383
00:22:58,664 --> 00:23:00,791
Next to him, a display case
with a missing pendant

384
00:23:00,916 --> 00:23:03,002
worth over $200,000.

385
00:23:03,586 --> 00:23:06,547
The night of the murder Montero was
supposed to meet a prospective buyer.

386
00:23:07,131 --> 00:23:09,717
- First, we thought the missing pendant...
- Hightower.

387
00:23:09,967 --> 00:23:12,803
"We need to talk in private.
I'll meet you in my perch."

388
00:23:13,137 --> 00:23:15,764
I don't have time now, Jane.
I'm in the middle of a briefing.

389
00:23:16,098 --> 00:23:17,808
Yeah. I can see that.

390
00:23:20,019 --> 00:23:21,896
Montero was running guns
to South America...

391
00:23:22,021 --> 00:23:25,816
The Montero case has turned into
a high-priority murder investigation.

392
00:23:25,941 --> 00:23:27,484
I can't just walk out.

393
00:23:28,027 --> 00:23:31,030
I suggest you rethink what you can
and cannot do

394
00:23:31,155 --> 00:23:32,740
from this moment forward

395
00:23:33,157 --> 00:23:36,118
because I know who the evidence
is about to reveal as the killer.

396
00:23:36,577 --> 00:23:37,620
Who?

397
00:23:38,954 --> 00:23:39,997
You.

398
00:23:43,417 --> 00:23:45,377
As a matter of fact,
they were best friends.

399
00:23:53,617 --> 00:23:55,244
Montero's gun running operation

400
00:23:55,369 --> 00:23:58,747
supplied Johnson with the weapon
that was used to kill our fellow officers.

401
00:23:59,206 --> 00:24:00,249
We're working on the theory

402
00:24:00,374 --> 00:24:02,835
that whoever took out Johnson
also took out Montero.

403
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:06,255
Excuse me, agents.
Urgent matter at my office.

404
00:24:06,505 --> 00:24:07,673
So you're suggesting

405
00:24:07,881 --> 00:24:09,842
both murders were part
of a vengeance play?

406
00:24:10,342 --> 00:24:11,385
Yes, I am, sir.

407
00:24:11,969 --> 00:24:13,804
Somebody wanted
both of these men dead.

408
00:24:14,346 --> 00:24:17,766
"Johnson the cop killer..."

409
00:24:24,565 --> 00:24:27,651
It suggests our killer has strong...

410
00:24:34,741 --> 00:24:38,620
- Jane, this better be...
- Good. My sentiments precisely.

411
00:24:40,247 --> 00:24:41,290
Where'd you get that?

412
00:24:42,791 --> 00:24:45,252
I borrowed a key to the armory
from Lisbon's desk.

413
00:24:47,170 --> 00:24:48,213
Are you a killer?

414
00:24:49,172 --> 00:24:50,716
I don't know your game here

415
00:24:51,174 --> 00:24:54,887
but I don't have time to be taken on
one of your emotional joyrides.

416
00:24:55,137 --> 00:24:56,555
Not that I'm judging.

417
00:24:57,264 --> 00:24:59,725
Seeking revenge on men
that are responsible for the death

418
00:24:59,850 --> 00:25:02,978
of someone you love, it's a hobby
I like to dabble in myself.

419
00:25:03,186 --> 00:25:04,396
You think it's true?

420
00:25:05,063 --> 00:25:07,608
You think it's true that... that I killed
Johnson and Montero?

421
00:25:07,816 --> 00:25:09,651
Well, let's just say I'm open-minded.

422
00:25:11,987 --> 00:25:14,239
Any minute now, the lab
is going to identify your prints

423
00:25:14,364 --> 00:25:16,033
at the Montero crime scene.

424
00:25:16,366 --> 00:25:18,201
I have never been
to that museum.

425
00:25:18,744 --> 00:25:20,412
Well, then you're either
being framed...

426
00:25:21,413 --> 00:25:22,956
or you're a lunatic killer.

427
00:25:23,373 --> 00:25:25,250
In either case
you should phone your family

428
00:25:25,375 --> 00:25:27,502
'cause my guess is
the pot roast is gonna be served

429
00:25:27,628 --> 00:25:28,795
a little late this evening.

430
00:25:29,212 --> 00:25:30,672
If you don't point that shotgun
away from me

431
00:25:30,797 --> 00:25:33,300
I swear I will use it to beat you
like a rented mule.

432
00:25:33,508 --> 00:25:35,761
Spoken like a true lunatic killer.

433
00:25:36,345 --> 00:25:38,221
You're not giving me much
to work with here.

434
00:25:38,388 --> 00:25:39,431
I mean it.

435
00:25:40,057 --> 00:25:41,099
So do I.

436
00:25:44,686 --> 00:25:46,104
Did you kill those men?

437
00:25:47,481 --> 00:25:48,649
I have to know.

438
00:25:49,858 --> 00:25:50,901
Why, Jane?

439
00:25:52,069 --> 00:25:54,738
If you think I'm guilty,
turn me over to LaRoche.

440
00:25:56,448 --> 00:25:58,116
- I'll go.
- No.

441
00:25:58,784 --> 00:26:00,869
If you killed Todd Johnson
then you're mine

442
00:26:01,411 --> 00:26:03,455
and you're gonna lead me
straight to Red John.

443
00:26:04,581 --> 00:26:05,624
Red John?

444
00:26:05,832 --> 00:26:07,167
- What does this have to d...
- Todd Johnson was taken out

445
00:26:07,292 --> 00:26:09,294
because he knew
Red John's secrets.

446
00:26:10,295 --> 00:26:11,797
As if you didn't know that.

447
00:26:13,465 --> 00:26:14,716
And if you didn't know it

448
00:26:15,133 --> 00:26:17,636
the real insider
murdered Montero to frame you

449
00:26:17,761 --> 00:26:19,221
which brings us the full circle.

450
00:26:19,388 --> 00:26:21,515
Are you or are you not a killer?

451
00:26:24,226 --> 00:26:25,602
You know what I am, Jane?

452
00:26:29,439 --> 00:26:30,899
I'm a single mom...

453
00:26:31,733 --> 00:26:34,069
with two innocent children
at home.

454
00:26:35,737 --> 00:26:38,198
There's nothing in the world
I would do

455
00:26:38,448 --> 00:26:41,451
to compromise their safety
or their future.

456
00:26:45,330 --> 00:26:46,540
Please, Jane.

457
00:26:59,970 --> 00:27:01,263
I've heard enough to convince me

458
00:27:01,388 --> 00:27:02,889
that we're looking
for one killer here.

459
00:27:03,140 --> 00:27:04,558
J.J., you take lead.

460
00:27:06,018 --> 00:27:07,853
This is now
a double murder investigation.

461
00:27:09,563 --> 00:27:11,982
Excuse me, Director Bertram, I'm sorry.
Sorry, everybody.

462
00:27:12,107 --> 00:27:13,817
Um, you asked for developments
on the Montero case.

463
00:27:13,942 --> 00:27:15,027
I think this qualifies.

464
00:27:17,612 --> 00:27:18,989
This has to be a false positive.

465
00:27:19,156 --> 00:27:21,992
No, I checked and double-checked
all the bifurcations.

466
00:27:22,117 --> 00:27:23,994
- It's a clear match.
- What is it?

467
00:27:24,286 --> 00:27:25,328
A mistake.

468
00:27:25,579 --> 00:27:27,873
Hightower's prints
at the Montero crime scene?

469
00:27:28,123 --> 00:27:29,291
Yeah. I'm not surprised.

470
00:27:30,208 --> 00:27:31,793
Have another analyst verify
your findings.

471
00:27:31,918 --> 00:27:33,295
- Yes, sir.
- Van Pelt...

472
00:27:33,962 --> 00:27:36,381
start working on a search warrant
for Agent Hightower's home.

473
00:27:36,798 --> 00:27:38,425
Is that really necessary?

474
00:27:39,259 --> 00:27:41,720
She can always grant us consent.
She's in her office now.

475
00:27:41,845 --> 00:27:42,888
I'll call over.

476
00:27:43,263 --> 00:27:45,390
Contact the university police.
Find out if they have record

477
00:27:45,515 --> 00:27:49,478
of a vehicle matching Agent Hightower's
on campus the night of the murder.

478
00:27:49,770 --> 00:27:52,189
Ask them to check security footage.

479
00:27:52,522 --> 00:27:53,565
Yes, sir.

480
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:56,026
I don't like the way
this is being handled.

481
00:27:57,611 --> 00:28:00,447
Can we just take a moment
before we destroy a colleague's career?

482
00:28:00,697 --> 00:28:04,326
Agent Hightower has been on top
of a short suspect list

483
00:28:04,493 --> 00:28:06,286
in the Johnson murder for some time

484
00:28:06,661 --> 00:28:10,874
even before Director Bertram notified me
that she was romantically linked

485
00:28:10,999 --> 00:28:12,709
with one of his victims.

486
00:28:13,376 --> 00:28:14,795
Now you're into her sex life?

487
00:28:15,629 --> 00:28:18,215
Wow, when you boys decide
to destroy a woman's reputation

488
00:28:18,381 --> 00:28:20,050
- you really go all out.
- Lisbon!

489
00:28:20,425 --> 00:28:23,595
You're the one who just told me that the
Johnson and Montero murders were linked.

490
00:28:23,929 --> 00:28:25,263
Now we have evidence.

491
00:28:26,014 --> 00:28:28,141
If you're too close to this,
let me know

492
00:28:28,266 --> 00:28:30,060
and I'll move you off this investigation.

493
00:28:30,685 --> 00:28:33,188
- I'll be fine, sir.
- Hightower never went to her office.

494
00:28:33,313 --> 00:28:34,481
I just spoke to her assistant.

495
00:28:34,773 --> 00:28:38,568
That's my fault. I let her walk out.
I didn't think she would run.

496
00:28:38,860 --> 00:28:40,070
Who said she's running?

497
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:42,155
For all we know, she's in the ladies room.

498
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:43,406
Maybe you should check.

499
00:28:43,573 --> 00:28:47,327
We're going to conduct a search
of Agent Hightower's home and office now.

500
00:28:49,287 --> 00:28:51,623
"Leave your name and number.
I'll get back to you as soon as I can."

501
00:28:51,832 --> 00:28:54,793
It's Lisbon. Wherever you are,
do us both a favor

502
00:28:54,918 --> 00:28:56,670
and call me as soon
as you get this, okay?

503
00:29:09,099 --> 00:29:11,268
I can't believe we have
to go through the boss's stuff.

504
00:29:11,643 --> 00:29:12,769
Suspect's a suspect.

505
00:29:16,523 --> 00:29:18,817
Just feels so wrong, though.

506
00:29:26,199 --> 00:29:27,242
Wait a second.

507
00:29:28,618 --> 00:29:29,786
This drawer's too heavy.

508
00:29:32,789 --> 00:29:33,832
Check it out.

509
00:29:34,541 --> 00:29:35,584
False bottom.

510
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:41,006
The stolen pendant.

511
00:29:41,756 --> 00:29:42,799
Hey, boss.

512
00:29:49,181 --> 00:29:50,223
Oh, no.

513
00:29:55,562 --> 00:29:58,023
Seems we found your mystery buyer.

514
00:29:59,983 --> 00:30:02,402
Put an immediate B.O.L.O.
out on Madeleine Hightower.

515
00:30:02,777 --> 00:30:04,529
She's considered to be armed
and dangerous.

516
00:30:13,246 --> 00:30:14,706
- Where is she?
- Over here.

517
00:30:15,415 --> 00:30:18,376
You saw the suspect?
Details, please. Where? When?

518
00:30:18,668 --> 00:30:20,587
Uh, I was coming out
of the elevator after lunch.

519
00:30:20,754 --> 00:30:21,838
Where was the suspect headed?

520
00:30:22,339 --> 00:30:24,716
Uh, up the stairs,
which I-I thought was strange

521
00:30:24,841 --> 00:30:25,884
'cause it leads to the roof, right?

522
00:30:26,009 --> 00:30:27,886
Not just the roof.
It's where Jane works.

523
00:30:28,178 --> 00:30:29,930
- Has anybody seen him?
- Not since this morning.

524
00:30:30,513 --> 00:30:32,140
Cover the exits, all of them.

525
00:30:32,390 --> 00:30:34,100
Use whoever you have to out here.

526
00:30:50,909 --> 00:30:51,952
It's locked.

527
00:30:53,119 --> 00:30:54,162
Jane?

528
00:30:54,955 --> 00:30:57,540
- You in there?
- "Yeah, I'm coming out."

529
00:31:00,210 --> 00:31:03,880
"You're gonna have to stand back
and if you're bearing firearms"

530
00:31:04,047 --> 00:31:05,340
"please lower them."

531
00:31:06,508 --> 00:31:07,550
"Please."

532
00:31:23,566 --> 00:31:26,027
Stand back, or he dies.

533
00:31:30,490 --> 00:31:31,533
Let us pass.

534
00:31:35,328 --> 00:31:38,915
If you don't let us pass,
you can try to stop me

535
00:31:39,624 --> 00:31:42,711
but just know that my finger
will reflexively pull this trigger

536
00:31:43,086 --> 00:31:45,255
If I stumble or if I fall.

537
00:31:45,630 --> 00:31:48,383
- Agent Hightower.
- Don't beat yourself up, Teresa.

538
00:31:49,134 --> 00:31:51,011
There's nothing you could
have done to prevent this.

539
00:31:52,721 --> 00:31:55,056
I got myself into it,
and I'm getting myself out

540
00:31:55,223 --> 00:31:56,599
so clear a path.

541
00:31:58,226 --> 00:31:59,269
Everyone.

542
00:31:59,978 --> 00:32:01,563
Lower your weapons.

543
00:32:03,273 --> 00:32:04,316
Let 'em pass.

544
00:32:05,275 --> 00:32:07,193
- Walk.
- Walking.

545
00:32:10,488 --> 00:32:11,531
Go ahead, Cho.

546
00:32:12,866 --> 00:32:15,535
Make your move. Watch him die.

547
00:32:39,351 --> 00:32:40,602
Nobody move.

548
00:32:41,603 --> 00:32:43,396
Everybody just stay calm.

549
00:32:49,527 --> 00:32:50,570
Put the phone down.

550
00:32:52,364 --> 00:32:54,616
Put the phone down.

551
00:32:55,408 --> 00:32:57,535
- You heard her. Put the phone down now!
- Put it down!

552
00:32:59,704 --> 00:33:00,747
Okay...

553
00:33:01,247 --> 00:33:02,290
Here's how it is.

554
00:33:03,708 --> 00:33:05,168
We're exiting the building.

555
00:33:06,086 --> 00:33:08,671
If anyone tries to stop us,
I pull the trigger.

556
00:33:09,381 --> 00:33:13,134
If anyone in here calls anyone out there,
I pull the trigger.

557
00:33:13,468 --> 00:33:15,345
Do as she says.

558
00:33:15,845 --> 00:33:17,430
Let's go. Move!

559
00:33:44,999 --> 00:33:46,167
Hey, Jane.

560
00:33:47,544 --> 00:33:49,295
That wolf's tooth you gave my kid?

561
00:33:49,754 --> 00:33:51,881
Was a huge hit. Look at this.

562
00:33:53,591 --> 00:33:55,635
He drew this. It's for you.

563
00:33:56,344 --> 00:33:57,804
Kind of in a rush here, Jim.

564
00:34:03,685 --> 00:34:04,811
Hey, stop!

565
00:34:07,564 --> 00:34:10,233
Hey! Hey, hey! That's Patrick Jane!

566
00:34:19,715 --> 00:34:23,135
Cho, get a chopper up and notify every
available CBI field unit.

567
00:34:23,427 --> 00:34:25,388
I want visual contact
with the target

568
00:34:25,596 --> 00:34:27,723
- but maintain a safe distance.
- "Roger that."

569
00:34:28,266 --> 00:34:29,976
My car, you drive.

570
00:34:30,518 --> 00:34:32,311
I'm a poor driver at speed.

571
00:34:55,001 --> 00:34:56,043
I'm sorry.

572
00:34:56,460 --> 00:34:59,463
- About what?
- Your boss. You admire her.

573
00:35:00,464 --> 00:35:03,301
That's irrelevant.
We need to focus on Jane's safety.

574
00:35:04,427 --> 00:35:05,553
"All units be advised"

575
00:35:05,678 --> 00:35:07,930
"a single-vehicle traffic collision
on North Main."

576
00:35:08,306 --> 00:35:10,600
"Vehicle is a dark-colored
late-model SUV."

577
00:35:11,017 --> 00:35:13,644
Copy. We're en route.
30 seconds out.

578
00:35:26,324 --> 00:35:27,950
- Wait for backup.
- You wait.

579
00:35:29,243 --> 00:35:30,786
Hold all oncoming traffic.

580
00:35:39,962 --> 00:35:42,506
We've got a suspect missing.
Set up a 10-block perimeter.

581
00:35:42,632 --> 00:35:44,884
Notify the T.A.C. Team
and call an ambulance.

582
00:35:46,636 --> 00:35:47,678
What happened?

583
00:35:49,388 --> 00:35:51,182
She was unwrapping her hand...

584
00:35:52,058 --> 00:35:53,726
the moment I was waiting for.

585
00:35:54,393 --> 00:35:55,519
To crash the vehicle?

586
00:35:57,730 --> 00:35:59,940
It seemed like a smart idea
at the time.

587
00:36:02,610 --> 00:36:04,612
They think Jane may have a concussion.

588
00:36:04,820 --> 00:36:07,114
They've taken him
to the hospital for a CT Scan.

589
00:36:07,573 --> 00:36:08,991
I'm just thankful he's gonna be okay.

590
00:36:09,241 --> 00:36:10,576
And where are we at
with our manhunt?

591
00:36:10,826 --> 00:36:13,204
We have perimeter teams deployed
around the command post

592
00:36:13,329 --> 00:36:14,789
for 16 city blocks.

593
00:36:15,039 --> 00:36:17,458
U.S. Marshals have joined the hunt.
So's the FBI.

594
00:36:18,709 --> 00:36:20,795
They put Hightower
on their most wanted list.

595
00:36:21,420 --> 00:36:23,172
Such a tragic turn of events.

596
00:36:24,590 --> 00:36:25,883
Look, there are worse things
that could happen here

597
00:36:26,008 --> 00:36:27,718
than we have an open-and-shut case.

598
00:36:28,469 --> 00:36:30,054
It's a blemish, to be sure

599
00:36:30,554 --> 00:36:33,474
but at least we can close the book
on this ugly chapter at CBI.

600
00:36:34,892 --> 00:36:36,936
"And when thy little heart doth wake"

601
00:36:37,645 --> 00:36:40,648
"then the dreadful night shall break."

602
00:36:41,190 --> 00:36:42,233
What's that?

603
00:36:42,942 --> 00:36:45,027
Ah, it's just a... an old poem I like.

604
00:36:51,367 --> 00:36:53,202
William Blake, I believe.

605
00:37:06,048 --> 00:37:07,633
Why aren't you answering
your cell phone?

606
00:37:08,259 --> 00:37:10,094
- Is it ringing?
- For two hours.

607
00:37:10,469 --> 00:37:12,513
I'm sorry. I thought it was my brain.

608
00:37:13,389 --> 00:37:15,015
Doctor said it's to be expected.

609
00:37:15,141 --> 00:37:17,768
Of all people to use
to effect her escape

610
00:37:18,144 --> 00:37:19,687
why would Hightower choose you?

611
00:37:20,771 --> 00:37:23,274
Theoretically speaking,
I think it makes perfect sense.

612
00:37:23,983 --> 00:37:26,444
I'm isolated in the rafters,
I don't carry a weapon

613
00:37:26,610 --> 00:37:27,945
and I don't know any of that...

614
00:37:28,779 --> 00:37:30,740
hand-to-hand combat jive.

615
00:37:30,948 --> 00:37:33,242
I don't want theories. I want facts.

616
00:37:33,909 --> 00:37:35,161
Why would she come to you?

617
00:37:35,870 --> 00:37:38,247
You don't... honestly believe...

618
00:37:38,748 --> 00:37:41,792
that I had anything to do
with Hightower's actions tonight, do you?

619
00:37:41,917 --> 00:37:43,461
I honestly don't know what to believe

620
00:37:43,586 --> 00:37:45,463
but whenever you're in the middle
of something

621
00:37:45,713 --> 00:37:47,089
I have reason to doubt.

622
00:37:48,632 --> 00:37:51,635
- And I like Hightower.
- When in doubt, don't.

623
00:37:52,178 --> 00:37:53,220
Well...

624
00:37:53,721 --> 00:37:55,723
Whatever happened tonight,
I'm glad you're safe.

625
00:37:56,474 --> 00:37:57,516
Thank you.

626
00:37:58,058 --> 00:37:59,101
Hey.

627
00:38:00,644 --> 00:38:02,188
Thank you for coming
to my rescue.

628
00:38:04,315 --> 00:38:07,902
I guess I should express my appreciation
to LaRoche.

629
00:38:08,611 --> 00:38:10,196
Is he still out commanding the troops?

630
00:38:10,362 --> 00:38:12,198
No. He went home for the night.

631
00:38:59,411 --> 00:39:00,913
- Jane?
- LaRoche.

632
00:39:01,622 --> 00:39:04,625
You have a fluffy white dog
and an entire...

633
00:39:05,167 --> 00:39:07,586
house.
Are those hummel figurines?

634
00:39:10,422 --> 00:39:12,675
Yeah.
You find that amusing?

635
00:39:14,093 --> 00:39:17,596
Well, I just didn't picture you living
in an actual house.

636
00:39:18,055 --> 00:39:19,431
Where did you think I lived?

637
00:39:19,807 --> 00:39:22,601
In a burrow on a riverbank.
Somewhere like that.

638
00:39:28,983 --> 00:39:30,985
What can I do for you, Jane?

639
00:39:31,735 --> 00:39:32,945
You already did for me.

640
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:35,030
You let Hightower exit the building

641
00:39:35,155 --> 00:39:37,283
instead of shooting me
in the brain stem

642
00:39:37,408 --> 00:39:39,577
and for that, I'm thankful.

643
00:39:41,078 --> 00:39:42,621
How'd you know I drink scotch?

644
00:39:43,497 --> 00:39:44,540
You do?

645
00:39:47,167 --> 00:39:48,210
Thank you.

646
00:39:48,377 --> 00:39:49,420
It's my pleasure.

647
00:39:50,796 --> 00:39:53,257
It's too bad she got away, though, huh?
Hightower.

648
00:39:53,757 --> 00:39:56,093
Perimeter will remain in force
until we find her.

649
00:39:56,218 --> 00:39:58,137
May take a day or two days
but we'll find her.

650
00:39:58,304 --> 00:40:01,557
- She can't escape.
- Oh, she's escaped. I know it.

651
00:40:03,350 --> 00:40:06,604
Just like you knew I was wrong
about Hightower's capacity for murder?

652
00:40:07,146 --> 00:40:08,939
That's the counterpunch. Landed it.

653
00:40:10,232 --> 00:40:11,483
Are we kids or what?

654
00:40:12,651 --> 00:40:13,694
Yes.

655
00:40:14,653 --> 00:40:15,696
We are kids.

656
00:40:18,324 --> 00:40:19,992
Well, good night, Jane.

657
00:40:21,035 --> 00:40:22,077
It is a good night.

658
00:40:43,557 --> 00:40:45,392
Did it work? Right.

659
00:40:45,517 --> 00:40:46,685
- Yes, it did.
- Did it work?

660
00:40:47,436 --> 00:40:48,479
Okay.

661
00:40:49,396 --> 00:40:50,522
I can't believe it worked.

662
00:40:52,316 --> 00:40:53,359
"It will work."

663
00:40:53,651 --> 00:40:55,569
- "This is crazy."
- "Not at all."

664
00:40:55,819 --> 00:40:58,948
"Once they set the perimeter
you will be like a rabbit in a trap."

665
00:40:59,073 --> 00:41:00,574
"They will search every vehicle leaving"

666
00:41:00,741 --> 00:41:03,869
"except the car of the man
that is in charge so hurry, get in."

667
00:41:03,994 --> 00:41:06,705
"Okay. All right. All right. How long...
how long do I have to be in here?"

668
00:41:06,872 --> 00:41:10,501
- "Until you hear this."
- "Okay."

669
00:41:10,626 --> 00:41:12,378
"Turn your cell phone off
so they can't trace you."

670
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:15,130
- "Here. Take mine."
- "Okay."

671
00:41:15,422 --> 00:41:16,674
- "Whisper."
- "All right."

672
00:41:17,049 --> 00:41:19,176
- Here's your cell phone.
- Did you make arrangements?

673
00:41:19,677 --> 00:41:20,719
Yeah, I talked to my sister.

674
00:41:20,844 --> 00:41:22,888
She's waiting for me just outside
town with my kids.

675
00:41:23,222 --> 00:41:25,265
Perfect. You're gonna have
to completely vanish

676
00:41:25,391 --> 00:41:27,017
because if Red John finds out
where you are

677
00:41:27,142 --> 00:41:28,185
he will come after you.

678
00:41:28,310 --> 00:41:30,980
She has a cabin in Saratoga.
We can wait there for a few months.

679
00:41:31,146 --> 00:41:32,773
Perfect. He'll think he won this round.

680
00:41:33,148 --> 00:41:36,402
Red John has a insider at the CBI
who framed me for murder.

681
00:41:36,527 --> 00:41:38,278
I think it's safe to say he won this round.

682
00:41:38,654 --> 00:41:41,407
Yes, but now I have the advantage.

683
00:41:42,074 --> 00:41:44,994
With you gone, whoever it is
that works for Red John

684
00:41:45,119 --> 00:41:48,163
will start to relax,
and thus lead me straight to him.

685
00:41:49,456 --> 00:41:50,791
You risked a lot for me.

686
00:41:51,875 --> 00:41:53,377
Well, not for you entirely.

687
00:41:55,087 --> 00:41:56,672
I understand. Still...

688
00:41:57,840 --> 00:41:59,258
thank you for getting me
out of that building

689
00:41:59,383 --> 00:42:00,634
and back to my family.

690
00:42:01,301 --> 00:42:03,220
And thank you for not shooting me
in the face.

691
00:42:03,762 --> 00:42:07,099
No one can know about this.
This has to stay between you and me.

692
00:42:07,224 --> 00:42:08,809
Jane, you should at least tell Lisbon
what's going on...

693
00:42:08,934 --> 00:42:12,146
Nobody. He's too smart that way.
He'll sense a trap.

694
00:42:14,023 --> 00:42:15,441
I'm better off alone.

695
00:42:17,776 --> 00:42:20,112
Nobody is better off alone.

